course: dictionary
lesson: 3865
title: Frail: weak and easily hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frail means weak and easily hurt. A person can be frail because of old age or illness, and a thing can be frail if it is delicate and breaks easily.
explain: Look at the clues in «A sudden fright can make people fall or feel unwell, so never scare people near stairs or roads, or people who are frail or have a heart condition.» The sentence warns about people who could be hurt or made ill by a fright. Frail sits in that list with people near stairs and people with a heart condition, so frail people are easily hurt.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «or people who are weak and easily hurt». It still makes sense, so weak and easily hurt is a good meaning for frail.
fact: Frail means weak and easily hurt, often because of old age or illness.
fact: Frail can also mean easily broken or delicate, as in «a frail boat».
fact: Common phrases are «old and frail» and «frail health».
fact: Frail can be compared: frailer means more frail, and frailest means the most frail.
fact: A sudden fright can make a frail person fall or feel unwell, so always be calm and gentle around them.
exercise: What does frail mean? | Very loud and strong | *Weak and easily hurt | Bright and shiny | Full of fun and energy
exercise: Which thing is most likely to be frail? | A huge stone wall | A steel bus | A thick rubber ball | *A thin glass ornament
exercise: Which helpful action is good for a frail person on the bus? | *Offering them a seat | Ignoring them completely | Shouting at them to hurry | Pushing past them to get a seat first
test: Which word is closest in meaning to frail? | *Weak | Loud | Strong | Cheerful
test: Why should you never scare frail people near stairs? | Because frail people never move | *Because a fright can make them fall or feel unwell | Because they enjoy being scared | Because stairs are too short to be safe
exam: In «frail health», what does frail mean? | Covered in bright paint | *Weak and easily hurt | Noisy and busy | Very tall and wide
